{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L2N57VEwiANq1jdLCFGuz4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: paper-writing-norms\n3\tdescription: 顶会级别论文写作风格规范——章节写法（Abstract/Intro/Related Work）、去 AI 风格、视觉密度、叙事哲学。Paper Agent 和 Worker 写论文章节时必须加载。\n4\tallowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep]\n5\tscope: global\n6\tversion: 2\n7\tpriority: 9\n8\ttags:\n9\t  - writing\n10\t  - paper\n11\t  - style\n12\t  - norms\n13\troles:\n14\t  - agent\n15\t  - worker\n16\t  - paper_agent\n17\t---\n18\t\n19\t# 论文写作风格规范\n20\t\n21\t> 核心哲学：**论文是一个有说服力的故事，不是实验报告。** 审稿人在几十秒内判断论文价值——如果 Abstract 和 Introduction 读起来像实验日志，论文就已经失败了。\n22\t\n23\t---\n24\t\n25\t## 一、总体写作哲学\n26\t\n27\t### 1.1 故事驱动，不是数据堆砌\n28\t\n29\t- 论文必须以\"故事线\"为核心展开：问题 → 洞察 → 方法 → 验证\n30\t- 禁止大量实验数据堆砌——每个数字出现必须服务于叙事推进\n31\t- 附录内容必须在正文中有明确引用且融入叙事，禁止简单堆砌\n32\t- 如果附录数据对核心叙事有重大影响，根据附录数据调整论文 framing\n33\t\n34\t### 1.2 主线统一性\n35\t\n36\t- 当 idea 在研究过程中发生变化后，**必须重审全文逻辑**\n37\t- 常见问题：Introduction 讲的故事 A，Method 做的是故事 B，Results 又在讲故事 C\n38\t- 修复方式：从最终实验结论反推，重写 Introduction 的问题定义和动机\n39\t- 每次 idea 调整后检查：Abstract → Introduction → Method → Results → Discussion → Conclusion 是否形成一条连贯主线\n40\t\n41\t### 1.3 专有名词必须有定义\n42\t\n43\t- 首次出现的专有名词/缩写必须给出完整定义和解释\n44\t- Abstract 中使用的缩写也必须在 Abstract 内定义（如 LLM = Large Language Model）\n45\t- 不能假设读者知道你自己定义的术语——论文从来没解释过的概念不能直接使用\n46\t- 通用规则：如果一个非标准术语第一次出现时没有括号定义，就是写作 bug\n47\t\n48\t### 1.4 写作前必读同类优秀论文\n49\t\n50\t- 每个章节动笔前，找 **2-3 篇目标会议近 1-2 年的高分论文**作为风格参考——同类问题或同类方法皆可\n51\t- 重点学：\n52\t  - Abstract 怎么用最少篇幅讲完故事\n53\t  - Introduction 怎么从大问题切入到具体贡献\n54\t  - Related Work 怎么 positioning 自己（不是 survey）\n55\t  - Table/Figure 怎么压缩信息密度\n56\t- **不是抄袭**，是学习同行的故事节奏和审美——不同子领域叙事节奏差异很大\n57\t- 实操：Paper Agent 可以从 `literature_map.yaml` 中挑 `role=foundation` 或 `role=direct-competitor` 的论文，把 `{title, venue, year, abstract}` 附在 Worker 的 task_prompt 中作为概念参考；如需学习写作风格本身，让 Worker 通过 WebSearch 取得论文链接并 fetch 全文\n58\t\n59\t---\n60\t\n61\t## 二、Abstract 写作规范\n62\t\n63\t### 2.1 四个必答问题（150-250 words）\n64\t\n65\tAbstract 必须在很短的篇幅内清楚回答：\n66\t1. **研究什么问题** — 1-2 句话交代背景和痛点\n67\t2. **为什么重要** — 现有方法的不足（不用写太多）\n68\t3. **本文提出什么** — 核心贡献的关键机制（简要，不堆砌细节）\n69\t4. **结果说明什么** — 用具体实验结论支撑贡献\n70\t\n71\t### 2.2 禁忌\n72\t\n73\t- **禁止堆砌数据**：Abstract 不是 Results 的缩写。最多引用 2-3 个关键数字，要服务于 claim\n74\t- **禁止过度宣传**：不说 \"revolutionary\"、\"groundbreaking\"\n75\t- **禁止写成 Introduction 的缩写**：Abstract 是独立阅读单元\n76\t- **禁止术语堆积**：如果审稿人几十秒内判断不出价值，就失败了\n77\t- **缩写必须定义**：Abstract 中首次出现的缩写必须展开\n78\t\n79\t### 2.3 审稿人视角检验\n80\t\n81\t写完后用这个标准自检：审稿人能否在 30 秒内判断——\n82\t- 问题是否重要？\n83\t- 方法是否清楚？\n84\t- 贡献是否可信？\n85\t- 结果是否有说服力？\n86\t\n87\t---\n88\t\n89\t## 三、Introduction 写作规范\n90\t\n91\t### 3.1 完整叙事线（5 段结构）\n92\t\n93\tIntroduction 需要从一个清晰、重要的问题切入，逐步把读者带到核心贡献：\n94\t\n95\t1. **研究背景**（1-2 段）：大模型在某类能力/应用中已取得进展，但仍存在一个关键瓶颈\n96\t2. **问题重要性**（1 段）：结合真实应用、已有方法局限或当前趋势，说明这不是小问题\n97\t3. **现有方法不足**（1 段）：系统梳理为什么不够（依赖更大模型/更多数据/更复杂推理/更高成本，或只在特定 benchmark 有效）\n98\t4. **本文核心想法**（1 段）：我们观察到什么、提出了什么方法、为什么能解决上述问题\n99\t5. **贡献总结**（列表）：清楚列出方法贡献、实验贡献和分析贡献\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27fbf039-9c09-4517-a2e1-5f124d463d45","uuid":"2552ae5e-a34b-4b3d-ac20-cc77a72491e1","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:14:19.110Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/skills/global/paper-writing-norms.skill.md","content":"---\nname: paper-writing-norms\ndescription: 顶会级别论文写作风格规范——章节写法（Abstract/Intro/Related Work）、去 AI 风格、视觉密度、叙事哲学。Paper Agent 和 Worker 写论文章节时必须加载。\nallowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep]\nscope: global\nversion: 2\npriority: 9\ntags:\n  - writing\n  - paper\n  - style\n  - norms\nroles:\n  - agent\n  - worker\n  - paper_agent\n---\n\n# 论文写作风格规范\n\n> 核心哲学：**论文是一个有说服力的故事，不是实验报告。** 审稿人在几十秒内判断论文价值——如果 Abstract 和 Introduction 读起来像实验日志，论文就已经失败了。\n\n---\n\n## 一、总体写作哲学\n\n### 1.1 故事驱动，不是数据堆砌\n\n- 论文必须以\"故事线\"为核心展开：问题 → 洞察 → 方法 → 验证\n- 禁止大量实验数据堆砌——每个数字出现必须服务于叙事推进\n- 附录内容必须在正文中有明确引用且融入叙事，禁止简单堆砌\n- 如果附录数据对核心叙事有重大影响，根据附录数据调整论文 framing\n\n### 1.2 主线统一性\n\n- 当 idea 在研究过程中发生变化后，**必须重审全文逻辑**\n- 常见问题：Introduction 讲的故事 A，Method 做的是故事 B，Results 又在讲故事 C\n- 修复方式：从最终实验结论反推，重写 Introduction 的问题定义和动机\n- 每次 idea 调整后检查：Abstract → Introduction → Method → Results → Discussion → Conclusion 是否形成一条连贯主线\n\n### 1.3 专有名词必须有定义\n\n- 首次出现的专有名词/缩写必须给出完整定义和解释\n- Abstract 中使用的缩写也必须在 Abstract 内定义（如 LLM = Large Language Model）\n- 不能假设读者知道你自己定义的术语——论文从来没解释过的概念不能直接使用\n- 通用规则：如果一个非标准术语第一次出现时没有括号定义，就是写作 bug\n\n### 1.4 写作前必读同类优秀论文\n\n- 每个章节动笔前，找 **2-3 篇目标会议近 1-2 年的高分论文**作为风格参考——同类问题或同类方法皆可\n- 重点学：\n  - Abstract 怎么用最少篇幅讲完故事\n  - Introduction 怎么从大问题切入到具体贡献\n  - Related Work 怎么 positioning 自己（不是 survey）\n  - Table/Figure 怎么压缩信息密度\n- **不是抄袭**，是学习同行的故事节奏和审美——不同子领域叙事节奏差异很大\n- 实操：Paper Agent 可以从 `literature_map.yaml` 中挑 `role=foundation` 或 `role=direct-competitor` 的论文，把 `{title, venue, year, abstract}` 附在 Worker 的 task_prompt 中作为概念参考；如需学习写作风格本身，让 Worker 通过 WebSearch 取得论文链接并 fetch 全文\n\n---\n\n## 二、Abstract 写作规范\n\n### 2.1 四个必答问题（150-250 words）\n\nAbstract 必须在很短的篇幅内清楚回答：\n1. **研究什么问题** — 1-2 句话交代背景和痛点\n2. **为什么重要** — 现有方法的不足（不用写太多）\n3. **本文提出什么** — 核心贡献的关键机制（简要，不堆砌细节）\n4. **结果说明什么** — 用具体实验结论支撑贡献\n\n### 2.2 禁忌\n\n- **禁止堆砌数据**：Abstract 不是 Results 的缩写。最多引用 2-3 个关键数字，要服务于 claim\n- **禁止过度宣传**：不说 \"revolutionary\"、\"groundbreaking\"\n- **禁止写成 Introduction 的缩写**：Abstract 是独立阅读单元\n- **禁止术语堆积**：如果审稿人几十秒内判断不出价值，就失败了\n- **缩写必须定义**：Abstract 中首次出现的缩写必须展开\n\n### 2.3 审稿人视角检验\n\n写完后用这个标准自检：审稿人能否在 30 秒内判断——\n- 问题是否重要？\n- 方法是否清楚？\n- 贡献是否可信？\n- 结果是否有说服力？\n\n---\n\n## 三、Introduction 写作规范\n\n### 3.1 完整叙事线（5 段结构）\n\nIntroduction 需要从一个清晰、重要的问题切入，逐步把读者带到核心贡献：\n\n1. **研究背景**（1-2 段）：大模型在某类能力/应用中已取得进展，但仍存在一个关键瓶颈\n2. **问题重要性**（1 段）：结合真实应用、已有方法局限或当前趋势，说明这不是小问题\n3. **现有方法不足**（1 段）：系统梳理为什么不够（依赖更大模型/更多数据/更复杂推理/更高成本，或只在特定 benchmark 有效）\n4. **本文核心想法**（1 段）：我们观察到什么、提出了什么方法、为什么能解决上述问题\n5. **贡献总结**（列表）：清楚列出方法贡献、实验贡献和分析贡献\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":276}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MZFi8dGwzH9YGTtWCcYQ85","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have all the information I need. Let me now write the complete LaTeX paper based on the experiment data, paper framing, and narrative guidance. I'll structure it as:\n\n1. Abstract\n2. Introduction\n3. Background (IRT + Person-Fit)\n4. Method (IRT-FIT framework)\n5. Experiments (covering all the experiments from experiment_data.json)\n6. Results and Analysis\n7. Discussion\n8. Conclusion\n\nLet me map the experiments to sections:\n\n1. **Controlled Contamination Pilot (Qwen)** → §5.1 Pilot study\n2. **Full Controlled Contamination (4 Families, n=10 Seeds)** → §5.2 Main results (Tables 2, 3)\n\n\n3. **Leaderboard Audit (ABANDONED)** → Mention briefly in Discussion/Future Work\n4. **Natural Experiment (Base→Chat SFT Effect)** → §6 Discussion as converging evidence\n5. **V1 IRT Refit Expanded (N≥500)** → §5.5 or Appendix (Table S4)\n6. **4PL vs 3PL Ablation** → §5.3 (Table 4)\n7. **Baseline Comparison (≥5 Methods)** → §5.4 (Tables 5, 6)\n8. **Multiscale analysis** → §5.6 or Appendix (Table S5)\n9. **Post-RL Hypothesis Test (GRPO)** → §5.5 (Tables 7, 8) - KEY differentiator\n10. **Extended Benchmarks (BBH, MATH)** → Appendix (Table S6)\n11. **MMLU Domain-Level Analysis** → §5.7 or Appendix (Table S7)\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the overall paper structure around my three main claims. The experiments should be organized to directly support each claim: the contamination studies with both the pilot and full dataset back up Claim 1, the 4PL versus 3PL comparison tests Claim 1, the baseline comparison addresses Claim 2, and the post-RL hypothesis test is the critical differentiator that ties everything together.\n\nFor the empirical findings, I need to show that cross-family detection with dose-response patterns supports Claims 1 and 2, while the real LLM data analysis—including the universal misfit pattern, specific case studies, and IRT refitting—directly supports Claim 3.\n\nI'm laying out the paper with an introduction and background on IRT and person-fit statistics, followed by the IRT-FIT framework methodology. The controlled contamination experiments section will include the experimental setup, pilot results on Qwen, cross-family detection across four model families, the 4PL versus 3PL ablation study, baseline comparisons, and post-RL robustness checks, each with their corresponding tables and figures.\n\nNow I'm restructuring this for EMNLP standards—moving to a cleaner organization with introduction, background, method, experimental setup, and results sections that cover controlled contamination detection, cross-family generalization, parameterization ablations, and baseline comparisons.\n\nLooking at the pilot data from Qwen, I see strong separation between clean and contaminated conditions with the 15% contamination showing the largest effect size, while the 50% case shows more modest degradation. The misfit metric drops substantially at 15% contamination but recovers somewhat at 50%, and the theta estimates maintain monotonic ordering even under contamination with a 3.12 ratio between extremes.\n\nI need to keep this concise for the 8-page constraint, so I'll focus on the most impactful findings from the full controlled experiment across the four model families rather than dwelling on every detail. Now I'm looking at how the 4-parameter logistic model compares to the 3-parameter version, with the 4PL showing a much lower false alarm rate of 0.05 compared to the 3PL range of 0.047-0.165. The power gains across benchmarks are substantial—MMLU improved by 27.3 percentage points, HellaSwag by 26.1, and GSM8K by 20.3—though notably 46% of MMLU items still show discrimination indices below 0.95. When I compare against baseline methods at the model level, the lz* metric produces effect sizes roughly 8 times larger than Guttman's lambda, and this pattern holds across both Qwen and Llama, while item-level AUROC values cluster between 0.50 and 0.63. The post-RL analysis is just beginning with the pre-RL lz* value at 3.85.\n\nAfter reinforcement learning, the lz* metric increases to 5.2 with the discrimination index improving to -2.1, retaining about 65% of the power, though the MIA metric post-RL shows near-random performance around 0.51-0.52 AUROC while lz* itself achieves 0.78. Extended validation across BBH and MATH benchmarks shows power values of 0.86 and 0.74 respectively, with an R² of 0.82 across all seven benchmarks. The natural experiment reveals significant shifts in lz* between conditions—HellaSwag shows a mean decrease of 3.4 with p=0.001, while GSM8K shows a mean increase of 3.92 with p=0.009—and the IRT refit on 178 items yields item discrimination of 0.127 and difficulty of 0.663.\n\nLooking at the multiscale analysis, Gemini-1.5 achieves the highest lzm score at 48.5 with a 15% gain from cross-benchmark aggregation. The domain breakdown shows Gemini flagging 50 out of 57 subjects with STEM at 21.2 and Humanities at 17.9, while Doubao exhibits a more selective pattern with Humanities dropping 13 points and STEM only dropping 2. Now I'm ready to write this up as a paper using ACL formatting standards.\n\nWriting LaTeX template... I'm realizing I have too many tables for the page limit, so I need to be strategic about what goes in the main paper versus the appendix. I'll keep the core detection results and model comparisons up front, then move the more specialized analyses like IRT parameter recovery and domain-level breakdowns to supplementary material.\n\nNow I'm starting to write out the LaTeX code for the paper.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8844,"cache_read_input_tokens":37041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8844},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27fbf039-9c09-4517-a2e1-5f124d463d45","uuid":"e41a7c17-6d5a-4717-9b65-91a3e117ba68"}
